ALL MATCH: True

k in (#units = 6 + 6k):  k = 1 + r_E(t)/6 = 1 + (#zeta6-orbits of norm-t Eisenstein ints).
 r_E(t)=0  (t has a prime =2 mod3 to ODD power; t NOT Loeschian) -> 12 units (k=1)
 r_E(t)=6  (t Loeschian, single orbit: 3,4,9,12,...)             -> 18 units (k=2)
 r_E(t)=12 (t has a SPLIT prime =1 mod3, e.g. 13,21,31)          -> 24 units (k=3)
 => the unit-vector count is a TRIANGULAR-SIDE (Q(sqrt-3)) invariant of t,
    independent of the second CM direction sqrt(4t-1).
